IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-members`

-- coa3-part8-branch.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 8, Chapter 3 (Overseas branch registers):
-- ss 129 to 135; lines 1714-1785 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. See coa3-part8-members.l4 for how to read JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING.
-- It calls `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` from
-- coa3-part8-members.l4 for the limbs "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default".
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: s 1121 the officer is in default; paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 (s 134(3));
-- "Her Majesty's dominions" (s 129(2)(a)) is a plain fact the person states.

DECLARE `s 129 act under Chapter 3 of Part 8` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(1) the company gives notice to the registrar that it has begun to keep an overseas branch register`
    `s 135(3) the company gives notice to the registrar of the discontinuance`

-- ---- s 129: overseas branch registers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- gloss: "the countries or territories listed below" is a table of 26 names, two to a row; one string per cell, in reading order.
-- src:1717 | (2) This Chapter applies to—
-- src:1720 | Bangladesh | Malaysia
-- src:1721 | Cyprus | Malta
-- src:1722 | Dominica | Nigeria
-- src:1723 | The Gambia | Pakistan
-- src:1724 | Ghana | Seychelles
-- src:1725 | Guyana | Sierra Leone
-- src:1726 | The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China | Singapore
-- src:1727 | India | South Africa
-- src:1728 | Ireland | Sri Lanka
-- src:1729 | Kenya | Swaziland
-- src:1730 | Kiribati | Trinidad and Tobago
-- src:1731 | Lesotho | Uganda
-- src:1732 | Malawi | Zimbabwe
@ref s 129(2)(b) The countries or territories listed (src:1717 and src:1720-1732)
`s 129(2)(b) the countries or territories listed` MEANS
    LIST
        "Bangladesh"
      , "Malaysia"
      , "Cyprus"
      , "Malta"
      , "Dominica"
      , "Nigeria"
      , "The Gambia"
      , "Pakistan"
      , "Ghana"
      , "Seychelles"
      , "Guyana"
      , "Sierra Leone"
      , "The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China"
      , "Singapore"
      , "India"
      , "South Africa"
      , "Ireland"
      , "Sri Lanka"
      , "Kenya"
      , "Swaziland"
      , "Kiribati"
      , "Trinidad and Tobago"
      , "Lesotho"
      , "Uganda"
      , "Malawi"
      , "Zimbabwe"

-- src:1717 | (2) This Chapter applies to—
-- src:1718 | (a) any part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man, and
-- src:1719 | (b) the countries or territories listed below.
@ref s 129(2) Countries and territories to which the Chapter applies (src:1717-1719)
GIVEN `the name of the country or territory` IS A STRING
      `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(2) this Chapter applies to the country or territory` MEANS
    IF `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem `the name of the country or territory` `s 129(2)(b) the countries or territories listed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This Chapter applies to (a) ... and (b) the countries or territories listed below" (no "only")

-- src:1715 | 129 Overseas branch registers
-- src:1716 | (1) A company having a share capital may, if it transacts business in a country or territory to which this Chapter applies, cause to be kept there a branch register of members resident there (an “overseas branch register”).
@ref s 129(1) Overseas branch registers (src:1715-1716)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company transacts business in the country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 129(2) this Chapter applies to the country or territory` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) the company may cause to be kept in the country or territory a branch register of members resident there` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company transacts business in the country or territory`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if it transacts business in a country or territory to which this Chapter applies, cause to be kept there a branch register" (a grant or power with an "if" gate; fork F19)
    ELSE IF NOT `the company has a share capital`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company having a share capital"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 129(2) this Chapter applies to the country or territory`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a country or territory to which this Chapter applies" (a grant or power with an "if" gate; fork F19)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): s 129(2) lists some countries and territories without closing the list

-- "an overseas branch register": the branch register kept under s 129(1).
@ref s 129(1) The term "overseas branch register" (src:1716)
GIVEN `the register is a branch register of members resident in a country or territory, kept there under section 129(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) the register is an overseas branch register` MEANS
    IF `the register is a branch register of members resident in a country or territory, kept there under section 129(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cause to be kept there a branch register of members resident there (an “overseas branch register”)" (a defined term)

-- s 129(3) (a power to make regulations) and s 129(4) (negative resolution procedure) are machinery: coverage rows `inert`, reason 2.

-- src:1735 | (5) References—
-- src:1736 | (a) in any Act or instrument (including, in particular, a company's articles) to a dominion register, or
-- src:1737 | (b) in articles registered before 1st November 1929 to a colonial register,
-- src:1738 | are to be read (unless the context otherwise requires) as a reference to an overseas branch register kept under this section.
@ref s 129(5) References to a dominion register or a colonial register (src:1735-1738)
GIVEN `the reference is in an Act or instrument (including a company's articles) to a dominion register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in articles to a colonial register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the articles were registered` IS A DATE
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(5) the reference is to be read as a reference to an overseas branch register kept under s 129` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires" (a judgment the text leaves to the reader; fork F12)
    ELSE IF       `the reference is in an Act or instrument (including a company's articles) to a dominion register`
              OR (`the reference is in articles to a colonial register` AND `the date on which the articles were registered` LESS THAN Date 1 11 1929)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References (a) in any Act or instrument ... to a dominion register, or (b) in articles registered before 1st November 1929 to a colonial register"

-- s 129(6) is blank in this text (a row of dots): coverage row `repealed or blank in this text`.

-- ---- s 130: notice of opening ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1740 | 130 Notice of opening of overseas branch register
-- src:1741 | (1) A company that begins to keep an overseas branch register must give notice to the registrar within 14 days of doing so, stating the country or territory in which the register is kept.
@ref s 130(1) Notice of opening of overseas branch register (src:1740-1741)
GIVEN `the company begins to keep an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) the company must give notice to the registrar, stating the country or territory in which the register is kept` MEANS
    IF `the company begins to keep an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that begins to keep an overseas branch register"

@ref s 130(1) Within 14 days of beginning to keep the register (src:1741)
GIVEN `the date on which the company begins to keep the overseas branch register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130(1) the last day for giving notice` MEANS
    `the date on which the company begins to keep the overseas branch register` PLUS 14 -- "within 14 days of doing so": the 14th day after it

@ref s 130(1) Within 14 days of beginning to keep the register (src:1741)
GIVEN `the date on which the company begins to keep the overseas branch register` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) the company gave notice within 14 days` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` LESS THAN `the date on which the company begins to keep the overseas branch register`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 130(1) counts from the day the company begins to keep the register; notice before that day is not mentioned
    ELSE IF `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` AT MOST `s 130(1) the last day for giving notice` `the date on which the company begins to keep the overseas branch register`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days of doing so"

@ref s 130(1) Within 14 days of beginning to keep the register (src:1741)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 129 act under Chapter 3 of Part 8`
`s 130(1) the company must give notice to the registrar within 14 days (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 130(1) the company gives notice to the registrar that it has begun to keep an overseas branch register`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give notice to the registrar within 14 days of beginning to keep an overseas branch register"

-- src:1742 | (2) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:1743 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1744 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 130(2) Offence (src:1742-1744)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in complying with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1745 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 130(3) Penalty (src:1745)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 130(3) the penalty for an offence under s 130(2)` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 131: keeping of overseas branch register ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1746 | 131 Keeping of overseas branch register
-- src:1747 | (1) An overseas branch register is regarded as part of the company's register of members (“the main register”).
@ref s 131(1) An overseas branch register is part of the register of members (src:1746-1747)
GIVEN `the register is an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the register is regarded as part of the company's register of members` MEANS
    IF `the register is an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An overseas branch register is regarded as part of the company's register of members"

-- "the main register": the company's register of members, of which an overseas branch register is regarded as a part.
@ref s 131(1) The term "the main register" (src:1747)
GIVEN `the register is the company's register of members and not an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the register is the main register` MEANS
    IF `the register is the company's register of members and not an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company's register of members (“the main register”)" (a defined term: an overseas branch register is regarded as part of the main register, not as the main register)

-- s 131(2) (a power to make regulations) and s 131(3) (negative resolution procedure) are machinery: coverage rows `inert`, reason 2.

-- src:1750 | (4) Subject to the provisions of this Act, a company may by its articles make such provision as it thinks fit as to the keeping of overseas branch registers.
@ref s 131(4) The articles may provide for the keeping of overseas branch registers (src:1750)
GIVEN `the provision made by the articles is consistent with the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(4) the company may by its articles make the provision as to the keeping of overseas branch registers` MEANS
    IF `the provision made by the articles is consistent with the provisions of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the provisions of this Act, a company may by its articles make such provision as it thinks fit"

-- ---- s 132: the register or a duplicate kept available in the United Kingdom ----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1751 | 132 Register or duplicate to be kept available for inspection in UK
-- src:1752 | (1) A company that keeps an overseas branch register must keep available for inspection—
-- src:1753 | (a) the register, or
-- src:1754 | (b) a duplicate of the register duly entered up from time to time,
-- src:1755 | at the place in the United Kingdom where the company's main register is kept available for inspection.
@ref s 132(1) Register or duplicate to be kept available for inspection in UK (src:1751-1755)
GIVEN `the company keeps an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register itself is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a duplicate of the register, duly entered up from time to time, is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept available at the place in the United Kingdom where the company's main register is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(1) the register or a duplicate is kept available for inspection as s 132(1) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company keeps an overseas branch register`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that keeps an overseas branch register"
    ELSE IF       (`the register itself is kept available for inspection` OR `a duplicate of the register, duly entered up from time to time, is kept available for inspection`)
              AND `it is kept available at the place in the United Kingdom where the company's main register is kept available for inspection`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep available for inspection— (a) the register, or (b) a duplicate of the register duly entered up from time to time, at the place in the United Kingdom where the company's main register is kept available for inspection" (a bare "must"; fork F8)

-- src:1756 | (2) Any such duplicate is treated for all purposes of this Act as part of the main register.
@ref s 132(2) A duplicate is part of the main register (src:1756)
GIVEN `the document is a duplicate of an overseas branch register kept under section 132(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(2) the duplicate is treated for all purposes of this Act as part of the main register` MEANS
    IF `the document is a duplicate of an overseas branch register kept under section 132(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such duplicate"

-- src:1757 | (3) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:1758 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1759 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 132(3) Offence (src:1757-1759)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in complying with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1760 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 132(4) Penalty (src:1760)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 132(4) the penalty for an offence under s 132(3)` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 133: transactions in shares registered in an overseas branch register -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1761 | 133 Transactions in shares registered in overseas branch register
-- src:1762 | (1) Shares registered in an overseas branch register must be distinguished from those registered in the main register.
@ref s 133(1) Shares to be distinguished (src:1761-1762)
GIVEN `the shares are registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the shares must be distinguished from those registered in the main register` MEANS
    IF `the shares are registered in an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Shares registered in an overseas branch register"

-- src:1763 | (2) No transaction with respect to shares registered in an overseas branch register may be registered in any other register.
@ref s 133(2) No transaction may be registered in any other register (src:1763)
GIVEN `the shares are registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(2) a transaction with respect to the shares may be registered in any other register` MEANS
    IF `the shares are registered in an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No transaction with respect to shares registered in an overseas branch register may be registered in any other register"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares registered in an overseas branch register"

-- src:1764 | (3) An instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register—
-- src:1765 | (a) is regarded as a transfer of property situated outside the United Kingdom, and
@ref s 133(3)(a) An instrument of transfer is a transfer of property situated outside the United Kingdom (src:1764-1765)
GIVEN `the instrument is an instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(3)(a) the instrument is regarded as a transfer of property situated outside the United Kingdom` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is an instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register"

-- src:1764 | (3) An instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register—
-- src:1766 | (b) unless executed in a part of the United Kingdom, is exempt from stamp duty.
@ref s 133(3)(b) An instrument of transfer is exempt from stamp duty unless executed in the United Kingdom (src:1764 and src:1766)
GIVEN `the instrument is an instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is executed in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(3)(b) the instrument is exempt from stamp duty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the instrument is an instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An instrument of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register"
    ELSE IF `the instrument is executed in a part of the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless executed in a part of the United Kingdom, is exempt from stamp duty"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 134: jurisdiction of local courts ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "This section extends only to those countries and territories to which paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985
-- (which made similar provision) extended immediately before the coming into force of this Chapter." (a closed list: "only")
-- src:1775 | (3) This section extends only to those countries and territories to which paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (which made similar provision) extended immediately before the coming into force of this Chapter.
@ref s 134(3) The countries and territories to which the section extends (src:1775)
GIVEN `paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 extended to the country or territory immediately before the coming into force of this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(3) this section extends to the country or territory` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 extended to the country or territory immediately before the coming into force of this Chapter`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section extends only to those countries and territories to which paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) ... extended immediately before the coming into force of this Chapter"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985 is not among the sources

DECLARE `s 134(1) matter of jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `s 134(1)(a) to rectify the register`
    `s 134(1)(b) in relation to a request for inspection or a copy of the register`
    `s 134(1) another matter`

-- src:1768 | (1) A competent court in a country or territory where an overseas branch register is kept may exercise the same jurisdiction as is exercisable by a court in the United Kingdom—
-- src:1769 | (a) to rectify the register (see section 125), or
-- src:1770 | (b) in relation to a request for inspection or a copy of the register (see section 117).
@ref s 134(1) A competent local court may exercise the same jurisdiction as a court in the United Kingdom (src:1768-1770)
GIVEN `the court is a competent court in a country or territory where an overseas branch register is kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 134(3) this section extends to the country or territory` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 134(1) matter of jurisdiction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1) the court may exercise the same jurisdiction as a court in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is a competent court in a country or territory where an overseas branch register is kept`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A competent court in a country or territory where an overseas branch register is kept"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 134(3) this section extends to the country or territory`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section extends only to those countries and territories" (s 134(3))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 134(3) depends on paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER matter
             WHEN `s 134(1)(a) to rectify the register` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 134(1)(b) in relation to a request for inspection or a copy of the register` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 134(1) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names rectification and requests for inspection or a copy, and says nothing of other matters

DECLARE `s 134(2) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 134(2)(a) refusing inspection or failing to provide a copy of the register`
    `s 134(2)(b) making a false, misleading or deceptive statement in a request for inspection or a copy`
    `s 134(2) another offence`

-- src:1771 | (2) The offences—
-- src:1772 | (a) of refusing inspection or failing to provide a copy of the register (see section 118), and
-- src:1773 | (b) of making a false, misleading or deceptive statement in a request for inspection or a copy (see section 119),
-- src:1774 | may be prosecuted summarily before any tribunal having summary criminal jurisdiction in the country or territory where the register is kept.
@ref s 134(2) Summary prosecution before a local tribunal (src:1771-1774)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 134(2) offence`
      `the tribunal has summary criminal jurisdiction in the country or territory where the register is kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 134(3) this section extends to the country or territory` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(2) the offence may be prosecuted summarily before the tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 134(3) this section extends to the country or territory`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section extends only to those countries and territories" (s 134(3))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 134(3) depends on paragraph 3 of Schedule 14 to the Companies Act 1985
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the tribunal has summary criminal jurisdiction in the country or territory where the register is kept`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any tribunal having summary criminal jurisdiction in the country or territory where the register is kept"
        ELSE CONSIDER offence
             WHEN `s 134(2)(a) refusing inspection or failing to provide a copy of the register` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 134(2)(b) making a false, misleading or deceptive statement in a request for inspection or a copy` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 134(2) another offence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the offences of ss 118 and 119 and says nothing of others

-- ---- s 135: discontinuance of overseas branch register -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1776 | 135 Discontinuance of overseas branch register
-- src:1777 | (1) A company may discontinue an overseas branch register.
@ref s 135(1) A company may discontinue an overseas branch register (src:1776-1777)
GIVEN `the register is an overseas branch register of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(1) the company may discontinue the overseas branch register` MEANS
    IF `the register is an overseas branch register of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may discontinue an overseas branch register"

DECLARE `s 135(2) where the entries are transferred` IS ONE OF
    `s 135(2)(a) to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory`
    `s 135(2)(b) to the main register`
    `s 135(2) somewhere else`

-- src:1778 | (2) If it does so all the entries in that register must be transferred—
-- src:1779 | (a) to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory, or
-- src:1780 | (b) to the main register.
@ref s 135(2) Where the entries must be transferred (src:1778-1780)
GIVEN `the company discontinues an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN
      destination IS A `s 135(2) where the entries are transferred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(2) all the entries in the register must be transferred to the destination` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company discontinues an overseas branch register`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it does so all the entries in that register must be transferred"
    ELSE CONSIDER destination
         WHEN `s 135(2)(a) to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 135(2)(b) to the main register` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 135(2) somewhere else` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all the entries in that register must be transferred— (a) to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory, or (b) to the main register" (a bare "must"; fork F8)

-- src:1781 | (3) The company must give notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance.
@ref s 135(3) Notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance (src:1781)
GIVEN `the date of the discontinuance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 135(3) the last day for giving notice of the discontinuance` MEANS
    `the date of the discontinuance` PLUS 14 -- "within 14 days of the discontinuance": the 14th day after it

@ref s 135(3) Notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance (src:1781)
GIVEN `the date of the discontinuance` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(3) the company gave notice within 14 days of the discontinuance` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` LESS THAN `the date of the discontinuance`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 135(3) counts from the discontinuance; notice before it is not mentioned
    ELSE IF `the date on which the company gives notice to the registrar` AT MOST `s 135(3) the last day for giving notice of the discontinuance` `the date of the discontinuance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days of the discontinuance"

@ref s 135(3) Notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance (src:1781)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 129 act under Chapter 3 of Part 8`
`s 135(3) the company must give notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 135(3) the company gives notice to the registrar of the discontinuance`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give notice to the registrar within 14 days of the discontinuance"

-- src:1782 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (3), an offence is committed by—
-- src:1783 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1784 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 135(4) Offence (src:1782-1784)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in complying with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1785 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
